        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "de884aab-9c08-37b0-ac6b-218c8e0481d2",
                "word": "Empyrée",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "cf4850b8-c1ce-45ee-81f8-90675f1c34ee",
                        "entry_id": "de884aab-9c08-37b0-ac6b-218c8e0481d2",
                        "tags": [
                            "Plus rare"
                        ],
                        "form": "empirée"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "02710a07-8013-40f6-8d08-781b019037b7",
                        "entry_id": "de884aab-9c08-37b0-ac6b-218c8e0481d2",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "empyrée"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "55407eaf-7902-352c-ab84-1af396e50c76",
                        "entry_id": "de884aab-9c08-37b0-ac6b-218c8e0481d2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dans la cosmologie grecque, la plus élevée des sphères concentriques du ciel. Il était supposé être constituée des feux célestes, des planètes, et les dieux y habitaient."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a50f9ffc-7f48-4b56-b20c-51099a1c3fb3",
                                "sense_id": "55407eaf-7902-352c-ab84-1af396e50c76",
                                "text": "Vous ne pensez pas sans doute, comme la plupart de ces moricauds, que Brahma et Wichnou vont descendre de l’Empyrée pour jeter les Anglais à la mer."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "224c2084-b40b-4271-9f72-8fca872f3d3b",
                        "source_entry_id": "de884aab-9c08-37b0-ac6b-218c8e0481d2",
                        "source_sense_id": "55407eaf-7902-352c-ab84-1af396e50c76",
                        "target_lang_word": "empyrean",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "empyrean",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab9c7623-fefa-39fc-8de5-b52b4ba9d2c7",
                                        "entry_id": "a46a9e49-5ecf-3eaf-aecb-cf36b977476e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The highest heaven, supposed by the ancients to be a region of pure light and fire or else composed of ether, and sometimes seen as the dwelling-place of God or other divine beings; the highest celestial sphere according to ancient and medieval astronomy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8412759e-0bf4-46cb-addc-df3fb4976b0a",
                                                "sense_id": "ab9c7623-fefa-39fc-8de5-b52b4ba9d2c7",
                                                "text": "Perchance they mark\nWhere India's cliffs the trembling cloud invade,\nOr Andes with his fiery banner flouts\nThe empyrean,..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25573238-4deb-41b7-9982-f47d5d1fe0f2",
                                                "sense_id": "ab9c7623-fefa-39fc-8de5-b52b4ba9d2c7",
                                                "text": "So ſung they, and the Empyrean rung,\nWith Halleluiahs: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0720bdfa-e774-4183-a7e5-5fdd4420d34e",
                                                "sense_id": "ab9c7623-fefa-39fc-8de5-b52b4ba9d2c7",
                                                "text": "Milton, a name to resound for ages; / Whose titan angels, Gabriel, Abdiel, / Starr'd from Jehovah's gorgeous armouries, / Tower, the deep-domed empyrëan / Rings to the roar of an angel onset— […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "17d4650c-a20d-4cfd-bd73-677f13717196",
                                                "sense_id": "ab9c7623-fefa-39fc-8de5-b52b4ba9d2c7",
                                                "text": "I could have spoken in blank verse of Shakesperian beauty, all sorts of great ideas flashed through my mind; it was as though the bonds of my flesh had been loosened and left the spirit free to soar to the empyrean of its native power."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d466e2b6-13af-4b84-8b1b-86dcdfcad238",
                                                "sense_id": "ab9c7623-fefa-39fc-8de5-b52b4ba9d2c7",
                                                "text": "This particular evening, if it remembered for nothing else, will be remembered in that place for its strange sunset. […] The whole was so close about the earth, as if to express nothing but a violent secrecy. The very empyrean seemed to be a secret."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f1eea31-9616-4bca-81cb-609c203f959d",
                                                "sense_id": "ab9c7623-fefa-39fc-8de5-b52b4ba9d2c7",
                                                "text": "Like all religious thinkers, he carries with his scholar's equipment a pair of metaphysical wings, wherewith at any moment he may soar into the empyrean, out of reach of vulgar materialists, like you and me."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "empyrean",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b1ad9b82-bfc8-304d-a636-94195ca58e60",
                                        "entry_id": "16768607-d352-3ccb-9924-731ba596cf87",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of the sky or the heavens, and particularly relating to the highest celestial sphere in premodern cosmology; celestially refined."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f777aeb4-e95f-4db9-861c-4623773f48e7",
                                                "sense_id": "b1ad9b82-bfc8-304d-a636-94195ca58e60",
                                                "text": "In th' Empyrean Heaven, (the bleſs'd Abode) / The Thrones and the Dominions proſtrate lie, / Not daring to behold their angry God: / And an huſh'd ſilence damps the tuneful sky."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3aa6a338-efca-42de-a416-1e19dffce5f1",
                                                "sense_id": "b1ad9b82-bfc8-304d-a636-94195ca58e60",
                                                "text": "Yet upward she [the goddess] incessant flies;\nResolv’d to reach the high empyrean Sphere."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df02b3a7-b07b-4bc6-aff1-5211c5b79b0f",
                                                "sense_id": "b1ad9b82-bfc8-304d-a636-94195ca58e60",
                                                "text": "Lispings empyrean will I sometime teach / Thine honied tongue— […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "507f63fe-b434-4d5f-9049-d40c15e9726b",
                                                "sense_id": "b1ad9b82-bfc8-304d-a636-94195ca58e60",
                                                "text": "[…] it was like those gods of Epicurus, who saw the doings of men from their empyrean heights and had no might to alter one smallest particle of what occurred."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "b8a36cbf-8737-3ddb-b963-a4ef505f4d8b",
                "word": "empyrée",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "7870760e-fd8c-4754-ba3d-d3ceccd5115b",
                        "entry_id": "b8a36cbf-8737-3ddb-b963-a4ef505f4d8b",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "empyrées"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b740c74d-c333-3819-98e9-ae87e70c37a4",
                        "entry_id": "b8a36cbf-8737-3ddb-b963-a4ef505f4d8b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Variante de Empyrée, partie du ciel la plus élevée, que les anciens regardaient comme le séjour des divinités célestes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "84d09143-8938-4036-b0b2-ebcd438a147b",
                                "sense_id": "b740c74d-c333-3819-98e9-ae87e70c37a4",
                                "text": "[…] mais s'il consent à tirer de son arrière-boutique – le cabinet particulier comme il l’appelle – une bonne vieille bouteille, alors mon cher, on peut se croire dans l’empyrée."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7519730c-c7b1-4cb2-a096-e79e791e7172",
                                "sense_id": "b740c74d-c333-3819-98e9-ae87e70c37a4",
                                "text": "Enfants, dans vos yeux éclatants\nJe crois voir l’empyrée éclore :\nVous riez comme le printemps\nEt vous pleurez comme l’aurore."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e55fbfa5-d843-40af-8743-174bbaa31da0",
                                "sense_id": "b740c74d-c333-3819-98e9-ae87e70c37a4",
                                "text": "Il est un gros monsieur, là-haut, dans l’Empyrée… Nous le respectons fort ; quand il passe en nos rues, la croix en tête et la bannière, avec ses Oremus, nous habillons de nos draps blancs les murs de nos maisons. Mais entre nous…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0699807b-215b-4e24-bad3-4e4b02956262",
                                "sense_id": "b740c74d-c333-3819-98e9-ae87e70c37a4",
                                "text": "Il est vrai qu’à ce moment les applications du monorail se multipliaient, et l’anxiété de Tom n’était détournée des hauteurs de l’empyrée que par des menaces plus immédiates et des symptômes d’innovations plus rapprochées du sol."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bef64843-51c6-4e16-a948-2153d63f038d",
                                "sense_id": "b740c74d-c333-3819-98e9-ae87e70c37a4",
                                "text": "Il fuit son âme, l’âme immortelle et divine qui est en lui, il fuit son âme, créée pour l’amour, son âme plus belle que le septième empyrée…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c5593e7-ba72-4c7c-93d2-3d7d5789d134",
                                "sense_id": "b740c74d-c333-3819-98e9-ae87e70c37a4",
                                "text": "Le sanglier finit parfois aussi misérablement sur un étal ; mais jusqu’à son heure ultime, il résiste ; et il a souvent la joie posthume de se voir exposé intact, avec tous ses poils, chez Chatriot ou en quelque autre lieu de luxe ; car le sanglier ne quitte guère l’empyrée."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a928ec0-9423-4b5f-aeef-8aa175cf4f2c",
                                "sense_id": "b740c74d-c333-3819-98e9-ae87e70c37a4",
                                "text": "Les écrivains appartenaient à l’empyrée et leurs noms étaient Balzac, Hugo, Zola, Proust, soit des légendes et pas des hommes réels."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
